{
  "name": "iso29100",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "tag": "standard",
      "value": "ISO/IEC 29100:2024"
    },
    {
      "tag": "edition",
      "value": "2"
    },
    {
      "tag": "publication_date",
      "value": "2024-02-16"
    },
    {
      "tag": "replaces",
      "value": "ISO/IEC 29100:2011, ISO/IEC 29100:2011/Amd 1:2018"
    },
    {
      "tag": "iso_open_data_date",
      "value": "2026-11-05"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A LinkML model of the records an organization keeps when it applies the privacy framework of ISO/IEC 29100:2024 to the information and communication technology (ICT) systems that handle personally identifiable information (PII). The records say who takes part, which PII is involved and how it moves, what must be safeguarded and how, and how the organization stands against each privacy principle.",
  "title": "ISO/IEC 29100:2024 privacy framework records",
  "comments": [
    "The version is the edition the schema models, and source is ISO's page for it. ISO Open Data's records of the edition and of the two it replaced are copied to src/iso29100/schema/iso-open-data/ on the date the annotations give, and scripts/check_upstream_release.py reports when ISO changes them. The release tags are the schema's own versions.",
    "ISO/IEC 29100 is copyright ISO and IEC, and none of its text is reproduced here. An element's title and description are this project's own words. An element cites what it models by number in the iso29100_clause annotation only where a third party's public outline of the edition gives that number, so terms and lower subclauses go uncited. A reader with a licensed copy looks the text up there.",
    "Every record that other records refer to has a pf_id, and a reference holds that identifier. PfFramework holds each kind of record in a list of its own.",
    "The mappings to the Data Privacy Vocabulary (DPV) are the five rows DPV publishes for this edition, in upstream/dpv-iso.ttl, with DPV's direction kept. No other mapping is declared, because no source states one."
  ],
  "source": "https://www.iso.org/standard/85938.html",
  "see_also": [
    "https://lmodel.github.io/iso29100",
    "https://www.iso.org/standard/85938.html"
  ],
  "id": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso29100",
  "version": "2024",
  "imports": [
    "linkml:types"
  ],
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "prefixes": [
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "linkml",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/linkml/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "iso29100",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso29100/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "dpv",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/dpv#"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "schema",
      "prefix_reference": "http://schema.org/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "xsd",
      "prefix_reference": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
    }
  ],
  "default_prefix": "iso29100",
  "default_range": "string",
  "types": [
    {
      "name": "pf_duration",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso29100/PfDuration",
      "description": "A length of time as ISO 8601 writes it, such as P7Y for seven years or P30D for thirty days.",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso29100",
      "typeof": "string",
      "base": "str",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#duration",
      "pattern": "^P(?=[0-9T])([0-9]+Y)?([0-9]+M)?([0-9]+W)?([0-9]+D)?(T(?=[0-9])([0-9]+H)?([0-9]+M)?([0-9]+S)?)?$",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
